WEBVTT

cue0061039
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Absolutely. Of course.

cue0061040
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
I will go to the side now about all this.

cue0061041
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.000
You know. See when there are two aspects of law, of Jewish law that you must distinguish.

cue0061042
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
You have to distinguish between Jewish law and the politics of Jewish law, the business of Jewish law.

cue0061043
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.960
And the only thing I'm not, I, you know, unfortunately, unfortunately, I don't know anything about the politics and business of Jewish law.

cue0061044
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:44.540
But we're going to study today about the law, and we're going to see that they're quite simple, and they're very liberal, and they're very, you know, I think we should begin, yes?

cue0061045
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:54.920
Now, we're going to begin with, actually, it is the first holiday in Jewish history,

cue0061046
00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:01.260
because we as a nation began through the holiday of Passover.

cue0061047
00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.600
Now, to understand what Passover is all about,

cue0061048
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.840
we must remember that in the Tora we have two words,

cue0061049
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.240
and two different kind of rituals to commemorate that event.

cue0061050
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:21.740
One term is Pesaḥ. It's called Chagapesach. But also it is called Chagamasot.

cue0061051
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:29.920
It is a difference. It is a radical difference between what Pesaḥ is and what Masot is.

cue0061052
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.180
Pesaḥ, it refers to something very specific.

cue0061053
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:49.560
When the Jews were still slaves in Egypt, God destroyed in the last Makkah,

cue0061054
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.680
He killed every single firstborn of Egypt.

cue0061055
00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:01.020
At the same time that He was destroying or killing the Egyptians,

cue0061056
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:11.760
Passah al-Batteh Yiśraʾel. What's the word Passah means? Normally, they translate, and I don't know why,

cue0061057
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:19.860
they translate it as pass over, that God jump over. I don't know what it means to jump over.

cue0061058
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:26.520
I don't know what it means for God to jump over. I really simply don't know what it means to jump.

cue0061059
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.380
what does it mean to skip?

cue0061060
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.700
how God skipped something?

cue0061061
00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.720
I don't know

cue0061062
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.780
but I know what the word in Hebrew means

cue0061063
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.500
and not only

cue0061064
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.540
how do I know that this is the meaning

cue0061065
00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.040
because the Ḥakhamim say it

cue0061066
00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.020
early commentators

cue0061067
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:43.720
I'm talking about

cue0061068
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.900
1800-2000 years ago

cue0061069
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.320
they explain what the word Pasah means

cue0061070
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.620
Pasah means

cue0061071
00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.440
to protect

cue0061072
00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.740
and it is at the same time

cue0061073
00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.140
that God was killing the enemies of Israel?

cue0061074
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.960
He was protecting the Jewish people.

cue0061075
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.440
And it makes, there is a sense to it.

cue0061076
00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:05.240
How?

cue0061077
00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.200
Well, thousands and thousands of Egyptians were being killed.

cue0061078
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.760
I don't know, microbes, bacteria, viruses, I don't know.

cue0061079
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.520
And the Jews could have died from the death of the Egyptians.

cue0061080
00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:26.120
What happened is, at the same time that God was killing the enemies of Israel,

cue0061081
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:31.320
He was guarding every single Jew, yes, and protecting him.

cue0061082
00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:38.320
Passah al-Bateh Israel. Passah literally means, to protect.

cue0061083
00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.120
He was protecting the Jewish houses.

cue0061084
00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:49.620
Now, why, what was the structure of this protection?

cue0061085
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:58.120
God for first time, He asked us to do something which is psychologically terribly difficult.

cue0061086
00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:05.120
The Egyptians, just like the Indians for instance, they have the holy cow, an animal that they venerate.

cue0061087
00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:11.620
The Egyptians, they had the sheep, the sheep and the goat, the Gedi, yes?

cue0061088
00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.120
And they believed in it, they believed that this is a sacred animal.

cue0061089
00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:27.580
Now, the Tora says you have to bring as a Qorban, you have to sacrifice that animal.

cue0061090
00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:35.840
Not only that you have to sacrifice it, but moreover, you have to paint blood in the entrance

cue0061091
00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:45.640
of your house, yes, and the mezuzot, so that you are showing off to the whole world, not

cue0061092
00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.900
only that you did it, but you're not afraid.

cue0061093
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:57.540
Then there's another thing, and we're going to see how this develops into the holiday

cue0061094
00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.080
of Pesaḥ.

cue0061095
00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.480
Then there's another element.

cue0061096
00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.280
The Koran Pesaḥ has to be roasted.

cue0061097
00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:03.900
Why?

cue0061098
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:10.900
Why? Because if you ever roasted a sheep or a goat,

cue0061099
00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.900
then you see the smell goes to far distance.

cue0061100
00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.160
And therefore, again, the Jew was roasting this animal.

cue0061101
00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:28.860
Why? To advertise throughout the land that he was not afraid.

cue0061102
00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.100
and he was roasting

cue0061103
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.640
an object of veneration

cue0061104
00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.060
of the Egyptian

cue0061105
00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.160
now, one second, we'll see how things develop

cue0061106
00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.420
normally

cue0061107
00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.040
when you bring

cue0061108
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.520
a sacrifice

cue0061109
00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.420
you have to bring it in an altar

cue0061110
00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.300
you bring it in an altar

cue0061111
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.320
you need a Mizbeach

cue0061112
00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.280
there is no such thing as a sacrifice

cue0061113
00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.940
in Jewish or non-Jewish

cue0061114
00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.460
ritual

cue0061115
00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.360
which does not have an altar.

cue0061116
00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.360
And in the altar,

cue0061117
00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.780
you spill the blood of the victim,

cue0061118
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.260
you spill it in the altar.

cue0061119
00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.160
What happened?

cue0061120
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:08.940
Where was, there was no altar.

cue0061121
00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.020
Interesting is,

cue0061122
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.880
the altar was the house.

cue0061123
00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.080
And then, that's why,

cue0061124
00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.200
in the post houses,

cue0061125
00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.680
in the post doors of the house,

cue0061126
00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:20.400
you painted the blood.

cue0061127
00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.040
So it's interesting.

cue0061128
00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:23.640
Every Jew, in a sense,

cue0061129
00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.320
became like a priest, like a Kohen.

cue0061130
00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.400
The house,

cue0061131
00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:38.500
becomes a temple, and the post doors become the symbolic Mizbeah.

cue0061132
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.700
Now, one second, let's continue.

cue0061133
00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.200
We'll see how everything is going to fall into pieces and into places.

cue0061134
00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.400
Let's be logical.

cue0061135
00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.960
We are in Egypt.

cue0061136
00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:54.000
We are a defenseless minority.

cue0061137
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.620
We are slaves.

cue0061138
00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:08.620
And what does it make more sense? To smear the doorpost with blood and have the wrath of the Egyptian?

cue0061139
00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:17.620
Or to smear it, or not to smear it and have the wrath of God? Or put it differently,

cue0061140
00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:24.120
Would you risk an Egyptian bullet on the fact that God is going to protect you?

cue0061141
00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.120
Yes or no?

cue0061142
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.120
And that was, ran through the minds and the hearts of many Jews.

cue0061143
00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:35.120
We know, the Ḥakhamim say, that not every Jew brought Qorban Pesaḥ.

cue0061144
00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.120
That was, in a sense, the test.

cue0061145
00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:45.120
And the test means, I'm not afraid of man because I believe in the protection of God.

cue0061146
00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:53.120
And we did it. And because we did it, God passed on the house of Israel.

cue0061147
00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:58.120
You know, on those houses, God offers, offered His protection.

cue0061148
00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:04.120
And the fact was that not only no bacterias, no this, no harm, no sicknesses, yes?

cue0061149
00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.120
As they say later on,

cue0061150
00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:10.660
but nobody

cue0061151
00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.920
not even a dog

cue0061152
00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.580
their bark

cue0061153
00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.980
are the Jewish people

cue0061154
00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:23.760
we don't have

cue0061155
00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.240
but we don't have recording

cue0061156
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.620
the Ḥakhamim for whatever reason

cue0061157
00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:29.140
either there wasn't

cue0061158
00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.820
I would say probably there wasn't

cue0061159
00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:32.800
there were

cue0061160
00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:37.160
there was the protection of God.

cue0061161
00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.020
Nobody dared do anything.

cue0061162
00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.900
But then something very important comes out of it.

cue0061163
00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.840
The doorpost.

cue0061164
00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.400
In Hebrew called mezuzot.

cue0061165
00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:49.660
Alright?

cue0061166
00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.080
And here comes something like, out of this experience,

cue0061167
00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:57.580
this experience is transformed into something else.

cue0061168
00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.500
We have the mezuzah.

cue0061169
00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.560
What is the mezuzah?

cue0061170
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.080
what is the mezuzah?

cue0061171
00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.300
Chamin say

cue0061172
00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.880
there are ten times the name of God

cue0061173
00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:08.600
in the mezuzah

cue0061174
00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:11.400
Yotke Vake, which is the name of God

cue0061175
00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.440
appear ten times in the mezuzah

cue0061176
00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.560
because ten times

cue0061177
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.740
the name of God appear in Egypt

cue0061178
00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.200
how?

cue0061179
00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.560
in every single Makkah

cue0061180
00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.980
it was the name of God

cue0061181
00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.080
appearing

cue0061182
00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.820
in a very subtle way

cue0061183
00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.760
punishing the Egyptians

cue0061184
00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.940
and protecting the Jew.

cue0061185
00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:34.520
You see?

cue0061186
00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.600
Of course, the culmination is

cue0061187
00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.860
the tenth Makkah.

cue0061188
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.700
So, we have the mezuzah

cue0061189
00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.780
today.

cue0061190
00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.460
It is like an offspring

cue0061191
00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:48.140
of that concept

cue0061192
00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.400
that God protects

cue0061193
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.280
the house of the Jew.

cue0061194
00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.120
And that's why we put the mezuzah

cue0061195
00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.520
outside.

cue0061196
00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.620
How come that the mezuzah

cue0061197
00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.400
goes out? From the time of Moshe Rabbenu.

cue0061198
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:06.480
immediately after this, Moshe Rabbenu, like I don't know, a few months or a few, I don't know exactly when,

cue0061199
00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:15.560
but within that period of time, that's right, they began, yes, they began with the Musab Mizrah, it's an immediate Musab.

cue0061200
00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:25.500
Now what is interesting is this, that in the Mizrah also, some Jew says, well, better, I'm not going to show that I'm Jewish.

cue0061201
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.660
I'm not going to show that I'm Jewish

cue0061202
00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:29.600
why should I get in trouble

cue0061203
00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.060
and then alright fine

cue0061204
00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.660
but then you don't get the protection of God

cue0061205
00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.640
to get to obtain the protection of God

cue0061206
00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.440
you have to visibly

cue0061207
00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.780
show that you're not afraid

cue0061208
00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:43.240
of being Jewish

cue0061209
00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.940
and that's why the mezuzah

cue0061210
00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.360
the mezuzah has to be put outside

cue0061211
00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.320
in the street

cue0061212
00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.460
I mean

cue0061213
00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:52.660
in the part of the door

cue0061214
00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:53.880
which leads to the street

cue0061215
00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:59.680
that is, you cannot avoid it. I mean, unless you live in an apartment, alright.

cue0061216
00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:07.880
But in an apartment you have to put outside. So you're not afraid that your neighbors will discover that you're Jewish.

cue0061217
00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:15.880
So therefore, being almost, that experience almost defines what does it mean to be Jewish.

cue0061218
00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:21.080
On the one hand, there is concern to show off that you're Jewish.

cue0061219
00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.580
But if you don't show off that you're Jewish,

cue0061220
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.940
then you forfeit God's protection.

cue0061221
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.960
Or to put it vice versa,

cue0061222
00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:35.380
you must take a risk as a Jew in order to gain the protection of God.

cue0061223
00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.740
Do you understand this point?

cue0061224
00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:41.140
And the whole notion of Poseach, God Pasach,

cue0061225
00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:44.040
and this is Pesaḥ, is called also,

cue0061226
00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.700
because Pesaḥ means what I told you it means.

cue0061227
00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:47.620
Yes?

cue0061228
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:55.240
And that's why the Tora calls Pesaḥ

cue0061229
00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.200
Le'el Shemurim.

cue0061230
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.220
What do you mean the night of Shemurim?

cue0061231
00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.680
The night that you are protected.

cue0061232
00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.700
We are not afraid of anybody.

cue0061233
00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.620
May I just, a parenthesis,

cue0061234
00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.860
just a parenthesis, digression.

cue0061235
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.280
You see, there are some rabbis

cue0061236
00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:15.140
who although they died like four or five hundred years ago,

cue0061237
00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.760
I consider them as my teachers.

cue0061238
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.040
You know, I look up to them and I study them

cue0061239
00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.800
and I really try to do this.

cue0061240
00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.860
And one of those Ḥakhamim that I consider as a teacher

cue0061241
00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.980
is Rabbi Levi Shaul Mortera.

cue0061242
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.180
He was the Rabbi in Amsterdam.

cue0061243
00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.860
This is something very beautiful and very profound.

cue0061244
00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:38.460
He believes that whatever happened to the Jew in the past

cue0061245
00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:42.820
is a paradigm, yes, to whatever is happening to the Jew in the present

cue0061246
00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.100
and would happen in the future.

cue0061247
00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.440
That's why we don't write Jewish history,

cue0061248
00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.520
because Jewish history was written already.

cue0061249
00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:50.600
And those are the paradigms, you know.

cue0061250
00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:52.400
And he says something very, very interesting.

cue0061251
00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:55.200
He says, take the Pesaḥ, you know.

cue0061252
00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:56.140
Take the Pesaḥ.

cue0061253
00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:00.820
Now, of course, he was in a Christian society, in a Catholic society.

cue0061254
00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.620
I lived, I was born in a Catholic society,

cue0061255
00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.220
so I know what it means to live in a Catholic society.

cue0061256
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.180
If you ever lived in France, for instance, or Italy, or this, you know what I mean.

cue0061257
00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:16.760
You know, they're very, to put it mildly, they're very nasty, yes, when it comes to Jews.

cue0061258
00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:17.840
Very, very nasty.

cue0061259
00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:31.300
And it says, every Passover, they know, or they think, or they believe, rightly, wrongly, that we killed our God.

cue0061260
00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:35.400
they see us celebrating

cue0061261
00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.240
Passover

cue0061262
00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.760
Massah, eating the Massah

cue0061263
00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:40.860
drinking the wine

cue0061264
00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:44.160
in their hearts, they want to kill us

cue0061265
00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.200
they have the blood libel

cue0061266
00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.820
you know what the blood libel is

cue0061267
00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.560
because it happened to

cue0061268
00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.320
Syria, to Syrian Jews

cue0061269
00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:56.120
to both Shami and Halav

cue0061270
00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:58.120
it happened in Turkey, it happened in Saloniki

cue0061271
00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.300
